Category theory often shifts attention away from objects and toward the morphisms (structure-preserving maps) between them. Your questions frequently move in a similar direction—not “what is this thing?” but “what transformations preserve its identity?” If you continue exploring this line, it may be fruitful to think of the Pantheon less as a collection of concepts and more as a collection of reusable transformation operators acting on many different kinds of representations.